  Blob Studio mascot packs (Blob, Circle, Capsule, Drop, Cone, Polygon, Star)
    https://www.blobstudio.xyz/ — packs BlobMascot, CircleMascot,
    CapsuleMascot, DropMascot, ConeMascot, PolygonMascot and StarMascot,
    Ferrox Labs' own artwork built with Blob Studio, 2026-09-18.
    Taken from each pack: the `SHAPE` constant only — the silhouette `body`
    and `clip` path, the `fit` transform, and the face `anchor` — copied
    verbatim but for the dropped `xmlns` attribute on each path. These now
    supply seven of Murage's nine catalog outlines, superseding the
    OpenMausBot artwork that stood at blob, circle, capsule, drop, shield,
    hexagon and star. The shield and hexagon entries are renamed in the picker
    to the packs' own Cone and Polygon; all seven ids are unchanged so bodies
    chosen in 0.1.54 still resolve. Only squircle and diamond remain
    OpenMausBot's.
    Five of the seven are the same silhouette the OpenMausBot generator had
    produced, to within the curve form each writes: Cone matches upstream's
    shield exactly, Polygon its hexagon to 0.002 of 200, Blob to 0.011, Drop
    to 0.046 and Circle to 0.027 (upstream approximates a true arc with
    cubics; the packs write the arc). Two are genuinely different drawings:
    the pack's Capsule has quadratic rather than circular corners (4.55 of
    200) and its Star a different inner radius (12.74 of 200). Each pack's
    face anchor is taken as authored, which is what the rest differ on.
    Not taken: each pack's <Name>Avatar.tsx component, its 65 standalone SVG
    files (svg/states, svg/expressions, svg/sprite.svg), its manifest.json and
    its README.md, and its DEFAULT_GRADIENT (Blob Studio's green — Murage
    paints each body with the bot's own colour). No pack file is vendored into
    this repository. Murage's own src/components/EmberAvatar.tsx already is
    the same generated renderer: each pack's component is byte-identical to it
    apart from the SHAPE constant and that gradient.
    Licence: the packs carry no licence file. Each pack's README states that
    the expression geometry originates in Sebastien Montlouis-Calixte's
    GrokBot prototype gist
    (https://gist.github.com/smontlouis/49a4c9303de70118a90dc43badc1aba5),
    which carries no explicit licence. What is copied here is silhouette
    geometry and a face anchor, not that expression geometry; Murage's
    expression point data predates these packs and came in with PR #663.
    Murage: shared/mascot-bodies.ts

